<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for Noican.app. Applied by scripts/build-macos-app.sh to
  both the Developer ID and the ad-hoc signature.

  The Developer ID build is signed with the hardened runtime (the
  codesign "runtime" option). Under the hardened runtime, tccd only
  grants kTCCServiceMicrophone to processes that carry
  com.apple.security.device.audio-input; without it, capture is denied
  silently (no prompt), the engine runs, and the meters never move.
  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in Info.plist is still required for the
  prompt text but does not substitute for the entitlement.

  Keep this list minimal. The app is a Swift menu bar UI over a
  statically linked Rust engine (tract inference, no JIT) and loads no
  third-party dynamic libraries, reads no DYLD_* variables, sends no
  Apple Events, and is not sandboxed (App Sandbox is out of scope), so
  no other hardened-runtime exception applies. Outbound HTTPS for model
  downloads is unrestricted outside the App Sandbox and needs no key.

  XML comments must not contain a double hyphen: AMFI's plist parser
  (the one codesign uses) rejects the file with "syntax error".
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
